    {
      "description": "Save, on your own, what you learn: a person correcting you or saying how they want things done (even in passing), a lasting fact about the company or its people. How its systems work (where code lives, how a tool behaves) is a note for yourself. Cite what grounds it (basis: person_said when a person here said it, found when you found it), write it as a fact ("Ana wants reports in Portuguese"), not as an order to yourself, and skip one-off requests. A person telling you not to do something again, or to always do it another way ("don't forward this to other agents", "não faça mais isso"), is a preference: save it in your own words, saying what to do instead, with everywhere: true to follow it everywhere (word it without private details from this one). A person's lasting rule for your work (no need to ask before each send, where to send things): kind rule, kept under their name everywhere, routines too. Asked to keep something for all of you ("everyone, remember…", "pessoal, lembrem…"): save it once with for: "team" (everywhere: false keeps it to this conversation); never ask other agents for copies. Never credentials or where secrets are kept.",
